I've had this happen several times, mostly when there is a Real Nasty Critter
on the level (demon or something which wandered thru a polymorph trap).  This
is especially bad when the Bad Guys are clustered around the stairs leading
to the level; poor adventurers don't even get a move before they are pounded
by 4-8 demons, old pets, and ghosts.

The heroic method of fixing this is to carefully build up a character on the
first few levels who can take on the Bad Guys.  Note that killing several
demons with a low level character is a true test of Nethacking ability.

The wimpy method is to have a character enter that level and then Quit.
This will wipe out the bones level.

The sneaky method is to get the correct privs and "rm" the file containing
the bones level :-).

Anyone have any other ways to get past "killer bones levels"?

